INT. GUARD BOOTH - GRANGE COLD STORAGE - NIGHT

Rain is falling. MARA VOSS, thirties, stands at the door with her badge. She looks nervous.

MARA
I am so nervous about my first solo night shift. I really need this job. If I lose this job I don't know what I will do.

She holds her badge to the reader. It does not work.

DELACROIX, fifties, comes up behind her and opens the door with his own badge.

DELACROIX
Hello, Mara. I am Delacroix, your supervisor and the man who trained you. I have worked here for twenty-two years.

MARA
Thank you for letting me in. My badge is not working and that made me feel anxious.

DELACROIX
It happens all the time. Do not worry about it. Everything here is completely normal.

They go inside together.

INT. GUARD OFFICE - NIGHT

Mara hangs up her wet coat. There are four monitors. One of them is broken. A radio crackles.

OWEN (V.O.)
Hi Mara, it is Owen, the dispatcher. You are four minutes late.

MARA
I'm sorry, Owen. Delacroix had to let me in because my badge did not work.

OWEN (V.O.)
That is strange, because Delacroix is not supposed to be here tonight. He is off rotation.

MARA
That is strange. I feel like something is wrong here. I have a bad feeling about tonight.

OWEN (V.O.)
Try not to worry. Just do your rounds like normal.

MARA
Okay. I will do my rounds like normal.

She sits down and looks at the monitors for a while.

INT. COLD ROOM - AISLE FOUR - NIGHT

The room is very cold. There are blue pallets stacked up to the ceiling. Mara walks down the aisle with a clipboard and counts them.

MARA
One, two, three, four.

She keeps counting.

MARA (CONT'D)
Forty-one. But the manifest says thirty-eight. That is three more pallets than there should be. That is strange.

She writes it down on the clipboard.

MARA (CONT'D)
I should probably tell somebody about this.

She walks out of the cold room.

INT. GUARD OFFICE - NIGHT

Delacroix is sitting in Mara's chair drinking her coffee.

MARA
Delacroix, there are three extra pallets in aisle four. That does not match the manifest.

DELACROIX
Oh, that is nothing. Receiving stacks the overflow in aisle four when the dock is wet, and then nobody re-keys it into the system. It happens all the time.

MARA
Okay. That makes sense. Thank you for explaining it to me. I feel much better now.

DELACROIX
You are welcome. You should not worry so much.

MARA
You are right. I worry too much. That is one of my flaws.

Delacroix smiles and drinks more of her coffee.

INT. COLD ROOM - AISLE FOUR - NIGHT

Mara comes back into the cold room and looks at the pallets again.

MARA
I still feel like something is wrong. But Delacroix explained it, and he has worked here for twenty-two years, so he probably knows better than me.

She picks up the radio.

MARA (CONT'D)
Owen, it's Mara. There are three extra pallets and Delacroix says it is overflow. What do you think I should do?

OWEN (V.O.)
I don't know. Maybe just write it in the log and leave it for the day shift.

MARA
Okay. I will do that.

She writes it in the log and leaves it for the day shift.

INT. NORTH CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Mara walks down the corridor. Delacroix is standing in the dark.

DELACROIX
Mara, I have heard that you have been asking a lot of questions tonight.

MARA
I'm sorry. I did not mean to cause trouble. I just wanted to do my job properly.

DELACROIX
It is fine. But you should be careful. There are things going on here that are very dangerous. People could get hurt. The stakes are extremely high.

MARA
Okay. I will be careful. I do not want anybody to get hurt.

DELACROIX
Good. Goodnight, Mara.

He walks away. Mara stands there.

EXT. LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

A truck backs into bay three. Men load blue pallets onto it. Mara watches from the mezzanine.

MARA
That truck is not on the schedule. This is very suspicious.

She keeps watching. The truck drives away.

INT. GUARD OFFICE - NIGHT

Delacroix comes in and sits down across from Mara.

DELACROIX
Mara, I am going to tell you the truth. For six years I have been moving written-off stock out of this warehouse and selling it. I re-label the pallets so the lot codes do not match. I did it because my wife was sick.

MARA
I am shocked.

DELACROIX
I know. I am sorry you had to find out.

INT. GUARD OFFICE - LATER - NIGHT

Blue lights come through the window. Owen comes in with two police officers.

OWEN
I called the police an hour ago because I thought something was wrong.

MARA
Thank you, Owen. I am glad you did that.

The officers take Delacroix away. Mara watches them go.

EXT. LOT - DAWN

The rain has stopped. Mara and Owen stand in the parking lot with coffee.

OWEN
You did the right thing tonight, Mara.

MARA
I didn't really do anything. But I learned something about myself. I learned that I am stronger than I thought I was, and that I should trust my instincts.

OWEN
That is a really good lesson.

MARA
I think I am going to be okay here.

They drink their coffee as the sun comes up.
